.PP
Turbo C++, Borland C++ before 5.0, Watcom C++ before 11.0, Visual C++
before 5.0.
.PP
\f[CR]TRUE\f[R] and \f[CR]FALSE\f[R] always follow the chosen type, so
in C++ they are real \f[CR]bool\f[R] values, not integers.
.PP
\f[CR]bool\f[R], \f[CR]true\f[R] and \f[CR]false\f[R] are only defined
when the language has none of its own.
